{"step_index":1464,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:52:45Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:52:45+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:52:45+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/output_0d77a839.md`\nTotal Lines: 32\nTotal Bytes: 2342\nShowing lines 1 to 32\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Worker Output: 0d77a839\n2: \n3: ## Task\n4: Settle an open graph-theory conjecture in Lean 4: `(nontrivial) ⇒ (radius + 1) ≤ roman_domination_number` by proving `prove_e20263a9` in `Challenge_e20263a9.lean`.\n5: \n6: ## Mathematical Analysis & Settlement\n7: 1. **Direction**: Universally **TRUE** (`prove_e20263a9`).\n8: 2. **Computational Evidence**:\n9:    - 0 counterexamples across 1,252 graphs up to $n=6$ (all connected graphs).\n10:    - 0 counterexamples across all non-isomorphic trees up to $n=16$.\n11:    - 0 counterexamples across hundreds of random graphs and trees tested with MILP.\n12: 3. **Analytical Proof**:\n13:    - For Roman dominating function $f$:\n14:      - If no vertex has label 2: $\\text{weight}(f) \\ge |V| \\ge \\text{radius}(G) + 1$.\n15:      - If unique vertex $c$ has label 2: ball of radius 1 around $c$ contains $c$ and all vertices labeled 0. The complement has size at most $|V_1| = \\text{weight}(f) - 2$. By strict ball expansion, $\\text{ballWithin}(G, \\text{weight}(f) - 1, c) = V$, so $\\text{eccentricity}(c) \\le \\text{weight}(f) - 1$, implying $\\text{radius}(G) + 1 \\le \\text{weight}(f)$.\n16:      - For $|V_2| \\ge 2$: centers in a spanning tree are at distance $\\le 3$, yielding $\\text{radius}(G) \\le \\lfloor \\frac{3|V_2|-1}{2} \\rfloor + |V_1| \\le 2|V_2| + |V_1| - 1 = \\text{weight}(f) - 1$.\n17: \n18: ## Form