{"step_index":1486,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:53:27Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:53:27+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:53:27+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/reference/GraphInvariantsComputable.lean`\nTotal Lines: 537\nTotal Bytes: 27292\nShowing lines 501 to 537\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n501: Distance is not available to the kernel directly (`SimpleGraph.dist` is defined\n502: through `sInf` over walk lengths), so it is reconstructed as reachability. -/\n503: def ballWithin (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ → V → Finset V\n504:   | 0,       v => {v}\n505:   | (k + 1), v =>\n506:       let B := ballWithin G k v\n507:       B ∪ B.biUnion (fun u => univ.filter (fun w => G.Adj u w))\n508: \n509: /-- Eccentricity of `v`: least `k` with every vertex within `k` steps. -/\n510: def eccentricity (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) : ℕ :=\n511:   minUpTo (Fintype.card V) (fun k => ballWithin G k v = univ)\n512: \n513: def radius (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n514:   ((univ.image (eccentricity G)).min).getD 0\n515: \n516: /-- Undefined on a disconnected graph, where some vertex never reaches all of\n517: `univ` and `minUpTo` would fall back to `n`. networkx raises there. -/\n518: def HasRadius (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : Prop :=\n519:   ∀ v : V, ballWithin G (Fintype.card V) v = univ\n520: \n521: instance (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] :\n522:     Decidable (HasRadius G) := by unfold HasRadius; infer_instance\n523: \n524: /- ── graph construction from an explicit edge list ────────────────────────── -/\n525: \n526: /-- The graph on `Fin n` with the given edge list, symmetrised and loop-free.\n527: This is the shape the disproof exporter emits for a refuting witness.\n528: \n529: `SimpleGraph.fromRel` supplies the symmetry and irreflexivity proofs, so this\n530: stays a definition rather than a bundle of obligations that would have to be\n531: re-discharged (and re-adjusted across mathlib versions) in generated code. It is\n532: an `abbrev` so that `DecidableRel` synthesis can see through it at the use site. -/\n533: abbrev ofEdges (n : ℕ) (es : List (Fin n × Fin n)) : SimpleGraph (Fin n) :=\n534:   SimpleGraph.fromRel (fun u v => (u, v) ∈ es)\n535: \n536: end GraphCalc\n537: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
