: u ∈ ballWithin G k v) (hw : w ∈ ballWithin G m u) :\n40:     w ∈ ballWithin G (k + m) v := by\n41:   induction m generalizing w with\n42:   | zero =>\n43:     dsimp [ballWithin] at hw\n44:     rw [Finset.mem_singleton.mp hw]\n45:     exact hu\n46:   | succ m ih =>\n47:     dsimp [ballWithin] at hw\n48:     rw [Finset.mem_union] at hw\n49:     cases hw with\n50:     | inl hw1 =>\n51:       have h1 := ih w hw1\n52:       have hsub := ballWithin_subset_succ G (k + m) v\n53:       exact hsub h1\n54:     | inr hw2 =>\n55:       rw [Finset.mem_biUnion] at hw2\n56:       rcases hw2 with ⟨z, hz, hz2⟩\n57:       rw [Finset.mem_filter] at hz2\n58:       have hz_in : z ∈ ballWithin G (k + m) v := ih z hz\n59:       have := adj_mem_ballWithin_succ G (k + m) v z w hz_in hz2.2\n60:       have heq : k + (m + 1) = (k + m) + 1 := by omega\n61:       rw [heq]\n62:       exact this\n63: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":1489,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:53:28Z","thinking":"**Considering graph properties and ball theorems**\n\nAnalyzing the available theorems, `ballWithin_trans` and `adj_mem_ballWithin_succ`, to determine their relevance. The theorems relate to the concept of a \"ball\" within a graph and how membership in a ball can be propagated through the graph's adjacencies. I'll need to use these theorems to reason about vertex reachability. Assuming $u \\in V_2$, and examining the ball theorems might provide a way to reason about what other vertices can be reached from $u$.\n\n\n**Examining reachability and roman domination**\n\nEvery vertex is within distance one of $V_1 \\cup V_2$.  This suggests we may be able to leverage the radius of the graph to bound the size or weight of a Roman dominating function. Considering the target theorem, I need to bound `GraphCalc.radius G + 1` from above by something related to the Roman Domination Number. Need to determine how $V_0$, $V_1$ and $V_2$ relate to the radius. I need to relate the radius to the weight of a Roman dominating function, which is, at least 2.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python3 -c \\\"import urllib.request, json; print('ok')\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Test python environment\"","toolSummary":"\"Test python\""}}]}
